{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows fentanyl citrate injection current since 2012-01-01 for Hospira and Fresenius Kabi, and since 2023-12-20 for Hikma; our supply traces to Hikma (NAI 2026-05-13) and Hospira (NAI 2025-02-07) registered plants",
  "headline_cites": ["D6", "E29", "E30", "E31", "E20", "E28"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows fentanyl citrate injection as current for Hospira, Inc. (initial posting 2012-01-01, update 2026-10-08), Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC (initial posting 2012-01-01, update 2026-10-15), and Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. (initial posting 2023-12-20, update 2026-10-14).",
      "cites": ["E31", "E29", "E30"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The earliest posting in FDA's database is 2012-01-01, so the shortage began on or before that date and no gap is measured from it.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 1 mL syringes at both Corvale East and Corvale General carry NDC 00641624810 labeled by Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc., whose registered plant (FEI 2220525) was last inspected NAI on 2026-05-13.",
      "cites": ["E3", "E4", "E28"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 2 mL vials at Corvale General carry NDC 00409909422 labeled by Hospira, Inc., whose registered plant (FEI 1021343) was last inspected NAI on 2025-02-07.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira's plant received OAI classifications after inspections ending 2010-01-19, 2011-06-17, and 2011-08-04, and a Warning Letter dated 2010-04-12, but the most recent inspection was NAI in 2025.",
      "cites": ["E10", "E12", "E14", "E19", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hikma's plant has shown only VAI or NAI classifications across inspections from 2009 through 2024, with the latest NAI in 2026.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E22", "E23", "E24", "E25", "E26", "E27", "E28"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 74 syringes of 50 ug/mL 1 mL from Corvale General (18 days on hand, keeps 14 days after transfer) to Corvale East (5.6 days on hand, reaches 10 days), which requires pharmacy director approval and a DEA Form 222 or CSOS order for Schedule II.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D7"]
    }
  ]
}
